 (reinforcement learning).","targetRectangle":{"y":802.27369689941406,"x":184.11845397949219,"width":425.02500000000009,"height":155.24999848008156}},{"text":"Example-A computer first clusters patient data to find groups with similar health patterns using unsupervised learning. Then, using supervised learning, it predicts the likelihood of a specific illness within each group based on labeled cases of that illness in the past.","targetRectangle":{"y":222.22193908691406,"x":279.42166137695312,"width":540.70000000000005,"height":155.24999848008156}},{"text":"pasted-image.tiff","targetRectangle":{"y":1028.6756591796875,"x":1778.8485870361328,"width":118.83621215820312,"height":34.581336975097656}},{"text":"label-tag-with-white-details-and-string.png","targetRectangle":{"y":453.81490325927734,"x":1085.7316741943359,"width":96.993675231933594,"height":96.993675231933594}},{"text":"￼","targetRectangle":{"y":1049.9674994945526,"x":11.404099398001563,"width":20.015999999999998,"height":21.496002197265625}},{"text":"Reinforcement Learning","targetRectangle":{"y":874.12556838989258,"x":840.45402275491506,"width":285.85095739737153,"height":105.26865455356892}},{"text":"© Zahra Shakeri, Dalla Lana School of Public Health, University of Toronto","targetRectangle":{"y":1055.1609382629395,"x":54.743599891662598,"width":495.66000000000008,"height":16.580001831054688}},{"text":"Unsupervised Learning","targetRectangle":{"y":576.44829559326172,"x":1024.1139492206275,"width":262.15084018371999,"height":105.26865455356892}},{"text":"label-tag-with-white-details-and-string.png","targetRectangle":{"y":422.65032958984375,"x":729.76860046386719,"width":122.99440765380859,"height":122.99440765380859}},{"text":"Taxonomy of machine learning tasks","targetRectangle":{"y":65.156173706054688,"x":355.77163696289062,"width":1171.1399999999996,"height":60.19999635219574}},{"text":"Supervised Learning","targetRectangle":{"y":564.32224655151367,"x":705.14344646967947,"width":217.49279325641692,"heigh